<title>USA: CME January volume climbs 7.3 percent year on year.</title>
<headline>CME January volume climbs 7.3 percent year on year.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) said volume in January totaled 17,243,141 contracts, up 7.3 percent from the year-ago monthly level of 16,069,826 contracts.</p>
<p>Open interest at month's end stood at 6,457,104, up 4.3</p>
<p>percent from 6,191,849 at the end of January last year.</p>
<p>Major categories were as follows:</p>
<p>Futures (individual)   Jan 1997	% change	   Jan 1996</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   8,592,814	   +3.5	   8,303,302</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   623,969	   +2.8	     607,226</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   411,763	   -4.5	     431,105</p>
<p>  Swiss franc	    360,561	  +12.1	     321,668</p>
<p>  British pound	  240,245	   +0.2	     239,698</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar	   189,884	  +52.9	     124,219</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		1,686,147	   -4.2	   1,760,050</p>
<p>  Live cattle	    361,799	  +15.9	     312,150</p>
<p>  Live/lean hogs	 180,290	   +1.5	     177,584</p>
<p>Options on futures</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   1,889,560	  +19.4	   1,581,940</p>
<p>  Eurodollar midcurve  739,557	 +282.4	     193,421</p>
<p>  British pound	   55,503	  -79.7	     273,760</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   238,946	  +19.1	     200,680</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   174,927	  -11.8	     198,305</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  489,363	  -22.2	     629,295</p>
<p>  Live cattle	     55,299	   +7.3		51,535</p>
<p>Since January 1994 CME has counted in volume anything that creates or liquidates open positions including expired options and SIMEX mutual offset transactions cleared on the CME.</p>
<p>Excluding these transactions, CME &quot;pit traded&quot; volume for January 1997 totaled 16,107,742.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Derivatives Desk (312) 408-8750</p>
